RRQ - DERIVED ANSWERS (abbreviated to the scorable points), then compared
  1  certification = was this person prepared (awarded once on completing preparation);
     licensing = is this person currently fit to practise (time-limited, renewable,
     renewal conditional on CPD); appraisal = how is this person doing and what next.
     Certificate valid yet licence failed: the certificate records a past event and does
     not expire; the licence tests present fitness and can lapse, e.g. CPD not completed.
     -> supplied scheme agrees. 1+1+1+1 = 4. Sums.
  2  standard/practice, code/conduct, curriculum/content, each with its question; one
     difference between frameworks: scope, granularity or stakes (topic-01).
     -> agrees. 2x3 + 1 = 7. Sums.
  3  four uses = initial training, continuing development, appraisal, public
     accountability; requirements = alignment to what a programme prepares for; generosity
     and safety to admit failure; precision, evidence, consequence; a defensible public
     claim. Tension: candour vs consequence.
     -> agrees. 4+3+1 = 8. Sums. See advisory on 4 demanded / 3 payable.
  4  candour vs penalised candour; trusted appraiser vs distance; weakness vs strength;
     must settle in advance which purpose each conversation carries, else summative wins.
     -> agrees, including the scheme's instruction not to award "one document cannot hold
     both", which matches topic-04's Isore-sourced qualification. 4 marks. Sums.
  5  ten standards; each divided into knowledge and understanding / dispositions /
     performance and skills; indicators beneath the parts, observable statements of what
     meeting a part looks like. Not all evidenced alike because the ten mix knowledge
     areas (1, 2), practices (4, 5), a values area (3) and a subject-specific area (10),
     so they are not parallel.
     -> agrees. 1+2+1+1 = 5. Sums, and matches both clauses of the stem.
     TAUGHT? yes: topic-02 "### The domains the standards cover", "It is a mixture of
     kinds ... they cannot all be evidenced the same way", restated in topic-02's Summary
     and in unit-assessment's Unit summary.
     DUPLICATES RRQ-06 or RRQ-07? No. RRQ-06 asks what the three-part separation BUYS;
     RRQ-07 asks the three tests of an indicator. Partial overlap only: RRQ-05 pays 2 for
     naming the three parts and RRQ-06 pays 2 for the same triad restated as shortfalls.
  6  three distinct shortfalls (not knowing / not valuing / not able), different remedies,
     a single judgement hides which applies. -> agrees. 2+1+1 = 4. Sums.
  7  observable, specific to the standard, achievable under real conditions; easy to check
     tends to measure a proxy producible without the competence. -> agrees. 3+1+1 = 5.
  8  choose one indicator, collect evidence, judge the gap, plan one change, re-collect the
     same evidence; breaks = too many indicators, and changing the evidence not the
     practice; each break destroys the station-2/station-5 comparison.
     -> agrees. 5+1+1+1+1 = 9. Sums.
  9  any three of pupil work / observation / planning documents / pupil voice / teacher's
     own record, each with what it shows, what it cannot show, and fakeability.
     -> the supplied entry is a 3x3 mark allocation with NO model content. Recorded as an
     advisory blueprint deviation ("each with a model answer").
 10  a teacher does not bring a real problem to someone who reports on them; mentoring is
     the cheapest effective development mechanism; the loss is invisible; the school keeps
     the appearance without the function. -> agrees. 4 marks. Sums.

  ALL TEN SCHEMES SUM TO THEIR STATED TOTAL. Total RRQ marks 59.

ERQ - DERIVED OUTLINES vs the supplied analytic rubrics
  1  four-use identification + three features + the compliant-vs-effective objection.
     Rubric criteria match the demand. 4 criteria x 5 = 20.
  2  Integrative. Derived mapping: plans thoroughly -> S4 instructional planning,
     performance (strength); knows subject -> S1 subject matter, knowledge (strength);
     marks late -> S5 assessment, performance (gap); rarely changes approach when pupils
     struggle -> S4/S5 performance, using assessment to adapt (gap), with a possible S9
     disposition reading; warm but quiet room, four pupils answering -> S6 learning
     environment, performance (gap), dispositions sound. Priority: the participation /
     responsiveness gap, above marking punctuality, on pupil impact.
     The rubric's "Standard mapping", "Use of the three-part division", "Appraisal
     judgement" and "Evidence discipline" match that demand. Solvable from the ten-area
     list in topic-02 without the primary document.
  3  write / game / harden an indicator. Rubric matches.
  4  Nadia vs Kashif + system design + accountability objection. Rubric matches.
  5  province reform + mechanism + alternative + cost objection. Rubric matches.

